Ticket #4471 merged **412 unique reports**, but its reports describe two independent date
failures. Grouping uses the tenant's locale and booking form rather than the intake tag.

<Callout>
These are two distinct failures, recorded separately in
[parser issue #1](https://github.com/hjmro/megatask/issues/1) and
[hint issue #2](https://github.com/hjmro/megatask/issues/2).
</Callout>

## Problems found

### Parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser read every date month first. In a day-first tenant, a date such as 4/7 was
interpreted as 7 April instead of 4 July. This group contains **379 reports**.

### booking-v3 gives day-first tenants a month-first hint

booking-v3 printed `MM/DD/YYYY`. Its users typed dates in that order, while the tenant expected
day-first input. This was a separate form-hint failure affecting **33 reports**.

## Evidence from #4471

The following view reflects the export dated 4 October 2026. Its ticket-placement warning
describes the desk's original merge, before the separate GitHub issues above were filed.
The intake tags are guesses; the grouping uses tenant locale and booking form.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Resolution

The [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update)
reports that #4471 closed on **5 October 2026**, with a different outcome for each problem:

- **Parser — fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  [Issue #1](https://github.com/hjmro/megatask/issues/1) is closed as completed.
- **Hint — won't fix:** booking-v3 was retired.
  [Issue #2](https://github.com/hjmro/megatask/issues/2) is closed as not planned.

The issues preserve the two distinct causes and their report counts. The engineering update,
rather than the act of splitting the reports, supplies the reason for each closure.

